    <h1>Privacy Policy for Bingie</h1>

    <p class="effective-date">
        <strong>Effective Date:</strong> August 9, 2026
    </p>

    <p>
        Bingie ("Bingie," "we," "our," or "us") respects your privacy.
        This Privacy Policy explains what information we collect, how we use
        and share that information, and the choices available to you when you
        use the Bingie mobile application.
    </p>

    <p>
        Bingie is a television show discovery, rating, and review application
        that allows users to create an account, rate and review television
        shows, interact with other users, and keep track of television content.
    </p>

    <p>
        By using Bingie, you acknowledge the practices described in this
        Privacy Policy.
    </p>


    <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>

    <h3>Account Information</h3>

    <p>
        Bingie uses Google Sign-In to create and authenticate user accounts.
    </p>

    <p>
        When you sign in with Google, we may receive information associated
        with your Google account, including:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>Your name</li>
        <li>Your email address</li>
        <li>Information necessary to authenticate your Google account with Bingie</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        Bingie does not receive or store your Google account password.
    </p>

    <p>
        We may also store information associated with your Bingie profile,
        such as your username, profile information, or profile picture if
        those features are available and you choose to provide them.
    </p>


    <h3>Ratings, Reviews, and User Activity</h3>

    <p>
        When you use Bingie, we collect information that you choose to create
        or provide through the app.
    </p>

    <p>This information may include:</p>

    <ul>
        <li>TV show ratings</li>
        <li>Written TV show reviews</li>
        <li>Users you follow</li>
        <li>Ratings and reviews associated with your Bingie account</li>
        <li>Other interactions you make through Bingie's social features</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        Ratings, reviews, usernames, profile information, and certain social
        activity may be visible to other Bingie users as part of the app's
        social and review features.
    </p>

    <p>
        Please avoid including sensitive personal information in public
        reviews or other publicly visible content.
    </p>


    <h3>Push Notification Information</h3>

    <p>
        If you enable push notifications, Bingie may receive and store a
        device push notification token associated with your device.
    </p>

    <p>
        This token allows us to send notifications to your device. Push
        notification tokens are used for notification delivery and are not
        intended to personally identify you outside of the Bingie service.
    </p>

    <p>
        You can disable push notifications at any time through your device's
        notification settings.
    </p>


    <h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>

    <p>We may use the information collected through Bingie to:</p>

    <ul>
        <li>Create, authenticate, and maintain your account</li>
        <li>Provide your Bingie profile</li>
        <li>Save your television show ratings and reviews</li>
        <li>Save information about users you follow</li>
        <li>Display content you choose to share with other users</li>
        <li>Provide the core features and functionality of Bingie</li>
        <li>Deliver push notifications you have enabled</li>
        <li>Maintain the security and integrity of the service</li>
        <li>Detect spam, abusive content, or inappropriate activity</li>
        <li>Moderate user-generated content</li>
        <li>Respond to support requests</li>
        <li>Comply with applicable legal obligations</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        We do not sell your personal information.
    </p>


    <h2>3. Reviews and Content Moderation</h2>

    <p>
        Bingie uses automated filtering to help identify potentially
        inappropriate, abusive, harmful, offensive, or spam content submitted
        through reviews and other user-generated content features.
    </p>

    <p>
        Content submitted to Bingie may therefore be automatically analyzed
        for moderation purposes.
    </p>

    <p>
        Content that violates Bingie's rules, community standards, or other
        applicable policies may be blocked, restricted, flagged, or removed.
    </p>

    <p>
        Automated filtering may not identify every instance of inappropriate
        content and may occasionally identify acceptable content incorrectly.
    </p>


    <h2>4. Google Sign-In</h2>

    <p>
        Bingie uses Google Sign-In to authenticate users.
    </p>

    <p>
        When you choose to sign in using Google, Google processes information
        as part of the authentication process and may provide Bingie with the
        information needed to create or access your account, including your
        name and email address.
    </p>

    <p>
        Bingie does not receive your Google account password.
    </p>

    <p>
        Google's handling of information is governed by Google's own privacy
        policies and terms.
    </p>


    <h2>5. Push Notifications</h2>

    <p>
        Bingie may use Apple's push notification services to deliver
        notifications to iOS devices.
    </p>

    <p>
        When notifications are enabled, a device token may be generated and
        associated with your Bingie account or device so that notifications
        can be delivered.
    </p>

    <p>
        Bingie may use push notifications for features such as:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>New follower activity</li>
        <li>Activity involving your reviews</li>
        <li>Account-related notifications</li>
        <li>Other relevant Bingie app updates</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        You can control whether Bingie sends notifications through your
        iPhone or iPad notification settings.
    </p>


    <h2>6. Television Show Information and TMDB</h2>

    <p>
        Bingie may use third-party television data services, including
        The Movie Database ("TMDB"), to provide information about television
        shows.
    </p>

    <p>This information may include:</p>

    <ul>
        <li>TV show names</li>
        <li>Show descriptions</li>
        <li>Poster and backdrop artwork</li>
        <li>Release information</li>
        <li>Episode information</li>
        <li>Cast or other entertainment metadata</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        Third-party services may have their own privacy policies and terms
        governing their collection and processing of information.
    </p>

    <p>
        Bingie is not affiliated with or endorsed by TMDB unless otherwise
        specifically stated.
    </p>


    <h2>7. How We Share Information</h2>

    <p>
        We do not sell your personal information.
    </p>

    <p>
        We may share or process information with third-party service providers
        when reasonably necessary to operate Bingie.
    </p>

    <p>These services may include providers used for:</p>

    <ul>
        <li>User authentication</li>
        <li>Application hosting</li>
        <li>Database hosting</li>
        <li>Push notification delivery</li>
        <li>Television show information</li>
        <li>Security</li>
        <li>Content moderation</li>
        <li>Technical infrastructure</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        These providers may process information as necessary to provide their
        respective services and in accordance with their own applicable terms
        and privacy policies.
    </p>

    <p>
        We may also disclose information when we reasonably believe disclosure
        is necessary to:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>Comply with applicable laws or legal processes</li>
        <li>Respond to lawful governmental requests</li>
        <li>Enforce our policies</li>
        <li>Investigate fraud, abuse, or security incidents</li>
        <li>Protect the rights, safety, or property of Bingie, our users, or others</li>
    </ul>


    <h2>8. Public Information</h2>

    <p>
        Bingie includes social and user-generated content features.
    </p>

    <p>
        Information that you intentionally make available through these
        features may be visible to other users.
    </p>

    <p>This may include:</p>

    <ul>
        <li>Your username</li>
        <li>Your profile information</li>
        <li>Your profile picture, if applicable</li>
        <li>Your television show ratings</li>
        <li>Your written reviews</li>
        <li>Users you follow</li>
        <li>Other content you choose to share publicly through Bingie</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        You should consider what information you choose to include in publicly
        visible content.
    </p>


    <h2>9. Data Retention</h2>

    <p>
        We retain account information and associated content for as long as
        your Bingie account remains active or as reasonably necessary to
        provide the service.
    </p>

    <p>We may also retain certain information when reasonably necessary to:</p>

    <ul>
        <li>Comply with legal obligations</li>
        <li>Resolve disputes</li>
        <li>Prevent fraud or abuse</li>
        <li>Protect the security of Bingie and its users</li>
        <li>Enforce our agreements or policies</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        When an account is deleted, personal information associated with the
        account will be deleted or de-identified where reasonably possible,
        except for information we are required or permitted to retain for
        legitimate legal, security, fraud-prevention, or operational purposes.
    </p>


    <h2>10. Account Deletion</h2>

    <p>
        You may request deletion of your Bingie account and associated
        personal information.
    </p>

    <p>
        Bingie provides an account deletion option within the application.
    </p>

    <p>
        When you delete your account, Bingie will delete or de-identify the
        personal information and user content associated with your account
        that is no longer necessary for legitimate legal, security,
        fraud-prevention, or operational purposes.
    </p>

    <p>
        Deleting your Bingie account does not delete your Google account.
    </p>

    <p>
        If you experience an issue deleting your account, you may contact us
        using the contact information provided at the bottom of this Privacy
        Policy.
    </p>


    <h2>11. Your Privacy Choices</h2>

    <p>
        Depending on where you live, you may have certain rights regarding
        your personal information.
    </p>

    <p>These rights may include the ability to:</p>

    <ul>
        <li>Request access to information associated with your account</li>
        <li>Request correction of inaccurate personal information</li>
        <li>Request deletion of your account and personal information</li>
        <li>Obtain information about how your information is used</li>
        <li>Withdraw certain permissions where applicable</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        You may also control certain information and permissions directly
        through Bingie or your device settings.
    </p>

    <p>
        For example, you can disable Bingie push notifications through your
        device's Settings application.
    </p>


    <h2>12. Data Security</h2>

    <p>
        We use reasonable administrative, technical, and organizational
        measures designed to protect information associated with Bingie
        accounts.
    </p>

    <p>
        However, no method of transmission over the Internet, mobile
        application, database, or electronic storage system can be guaranteed
        to be completely secure.
    </p>

    <p>
        We therefore cannot guarantee the absolute security of your
        information.
    </p>


    <h2>13. Third-Party Services</h2>

    <p>
        Bingie depends on certain third-party services to provide its
        functionality.
    </p>

    <p>These may include services provided by:</p>

    <ul>
        <li>Google, for account authentication</li>
        <li>Apple, for iOS functionality and push notification delivery</li>
        <li>TMDB, for television show information and artwork</li>
        <li>Hosting and database providers used to operate Bingie's backend services</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        These third parties maintain their own privacy policies and may
        independently collect or process information when you interact with
        their services.
    </p>

    <p>
        We encourage you to review the privacy policies of applicable
        third-party services to understand their practices.
    </p>


    <h2>14. Children's Privacy</h2>

    <p>
        Bingie does not knowingly collect personal information from children
        in violation of applicable privacy laws.
    </p>

    <p>
        If you believe that a child has provided personal information through
        Bingie in a manner that violates applicable law, please contact us so
        that we can investigate and take appropriate action.
    </p>


    <h2>15. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>

    <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes
        to Bingie, our data practices, legal requirements, or operational
        needs.
    </p>

    <p>
        When we make changes, we will update the Effective Date shown at the
        top of this Privacy Policy.
    </p>

    <p>
        We encourage users to periodically review this Privacy Policy for
        updates.
    </p>


    <h2>16. Contact Us</h2>

    <p>
        If you have questions, concerns, or requests regarding this Privacy
        Policy or your personal information, please contact us.
    </p>

